WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 4.5 · People, Culture & Volunteers
Check-ins, performance and development

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Short, regular check-ins, started now between co-founders, do more than a yearly appraisal.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Check-ins are short, regular conversations about priorities, blockers and feedback. With a few objectives and development goals, they do more for performance than an annual appraisal, and they can start now, between co-founders.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Three conversations, kept apart

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:39.722
Check-in: Priorities, blockers, feedback both ways and next steps. Short, weekly to monthly. For example: The bakery founders spend fifteen minutes every Friday on what worked and what is stuck.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:52.904
Objectives and development: Progress on a few objectives and one or two development goals, quarterly or twice a year. For example: The baker co-founder's goal this year: learn to manage a budget, with the accountant adviser.

7
00:00:52.904 --> 00:01:04.693
Wellbeing: Workload, stress and support, with no judgement on performance. Whenever needed. For example: After a hard month, the bakery founders talk about rest, not sales figures.

8
00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:05.693
Why keep them apart

9
00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:11.367
1. Mixing these conversations makes people less open in all of them.

10
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:15.930
2. Problems surface early, while they are still small.

11
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:22.233
3. Each person sees how their work contributes to your objectives.

12
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.233
What they connect to

13
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:28.167
1. Your first annual plan: personal objectives link to it.

14
00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:32.730
2. Your role cards: expected results become the objectives.

15
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:39.404
3. A written procedure for performance concerns, agreed before you need it.

16
00:01:39.804 --> 00:01:40.404
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.404 --> 00:01:44.967
Relying on one annual appraisal and nothing else.

18
00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:49.900
Mixing personal objectives with organisational KPIs and programme indicators.

19
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:55.833
Raising performance concerns late, in public or without support.

20
00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:58.233
You design your check-in rhythm and objectives for one role.

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
